15 0 obj
<< /A 45 0 R /Alt (Panel A illustrates viral integration in cells, showing progression from viral infection and DNA repair in a normal cell to DNA damage, viral integration, oncogene activation, and cancer development. Panel B compares HPV integration types: type 0 \(episomal, no integration\), type 1 \(simple, single insertion\), and type 2 \(complex, multiple integrations\), each depicted with corresponding DNA and virus segment diagrams. A legend identifies key symbols used.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 28 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 46 0 R /Alt (Flowchart depicting a genome assembly assessment strategy for viral integration, showing stepwise creation of diploid reference genomes at three complexity levels, synthetic chromosome integration, generation of synthetic ONT reads, two genome assembly approaches, and evaluation criteria with a legend for chromosome, viral junctions, duplications, and breakpoints.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (Venn diagram labeled panel A shows overlaps of integration sites among three synthetic human papillomavirus \(HPV\) integration reads at levels 1, 2, and 3,\nwith intersection counts displayed. Panel B, shaded pink, demonstrates two Level 1 model structures with diagrams of chromosome and HPV16 integration junctions\nmarked by red arrows and genomic coordinates. Panel C, shaded green, provides Level 2 model structures depicting integration events C and D involving chromosomes and corresponding sequences. Panel D, in blue, illustrates Level 3 model structures E, F, and UDSCC2, showing integration on chromosome, multiple junctions, and marked repeats.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt (Panel A presents assessment criteria for genome assembly, showing an example of a PASS structure and a partial structure with their respective recovery fractions. Panel B displays a table comparing runtime and memory usage for six assemblers on whole and local assemblies of synthetic reads. Panel C is a grouped bar graph comparing whole genome assembly PASS structure counts for six assemblers, using three bar shades for different levels. Panel D is a similar grouped bar graph for local genome assembly PASS structure counts. A key beneath the graphs defines colors for each assembler and the bar shade levels.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 49 0 R /Alt (Infographic depicting the analysis of UMSCC47 cell line with previous datasets and genome assembly results. Diagrams include chromosome 3 with integration breakpoints, HPV16 junctions, and comparison of six genome assembly tools, highlighting copy number variation, sequence gaps, and the regions of integration per legend.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 40 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
